  "problem": "A study of body weight conducted on two age groups of women, X and Y, yields standard deviations of ${\\sigma }_{x}=8\\,\\text{lb}$ and ${\\sigma }_{y}=10\\,\\text{lb},$ respectively.\nA researcher wants to determine whether the population mean ${\\mu }_{x}$ of the weights of group X is smaller than the population mean ${\\mu }_{y}$ of the weights of group Y. She decides to construct a $90%$ confidence interval for the difference between the population means.\n\nThe researcher sampled $50$ women from group X and $55$ from group Y, finding that their mean weights are $58\\,lb$ and $64\\,lb,$  respectively. Which of the following statements are true?  \n\nI. The end-points of the $90%$ confidence interval for the difference between the population means are approximately $-6\\pm 2.895.$\n\nII. All values contained within the $90%$ confidence interval are negative.\n\nIII. The confidence interval data suggests that ${\\mu }_{x}<{\\mu }_{y}.$\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $Z∼N(0,1),$ the table below shows the $z$-scores ${z}_{p}$ such that $P(Z>{z}_{p})=p$ for some particular values of $p.$*\n\n| $p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${z}_{p}$ | $1.282$ | $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |",
